WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:09.960
Coronavirus is dealing the Chinese
economy a very serious blow. The scope of

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:15.320
the virus' impact has already far
exceeded the 2003 SARS epidemic. This has

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:20.240
led to the virtual shutdown of China, the
world's second largest economy. That, in turn,

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.180
has disrupted global supply chains,
led to the collapse in international

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:28.740
commodity prices, and caused major
disruptions to the world travel industry.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.260
The marked slowing in the Chinese economy
is coming at a very bad time for the global

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:37.590
economy. Already before coronavirus, the
Japanese and German economies were

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:42.900
heading for recessions, Latin America was
being beset by widespread social unrest,

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:48.180
and the Indian economy was grinding to a
halt. Unless the corona virus epidemic is

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.350
soon brought under control, it is likely
that global economic conditions will

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:57.239
only worsen. That's bound to reach US
shores and bound to make a difficult for

00:00:57.239 --> 00:01:01.460
China to meet its commitments under the
US-China phase one trade deal.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.630
Unfortunately, it's far from clear that
the coronavirus epidemic is anywhere

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:12.689
near to being under control. How do you
think the corona virus will affect the

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:18.960
world's economy? Let us know in our poll.
Also, let us know what other topics you'd

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:25.619
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds
and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for

00:01:25.619 --> 00:01:30.680
more research and videos from AEI

